VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'that was more like pocketable that I could just bring around [music] with me on trips, just to get BTS, just to get photos and just kind of play around. There\'s something different, you know? The photography coming out of this camera [music] is incredible. Like being able'

[01:40] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'to shoot 50 MP photos. Keep in mind, 50 MP on this sensor is very different from 50 MP on a full-frame sensor. The 50 MP &gt;&gt; [music] &gt;&gt; on this one are pretty incredible. Some of the photos I get are just very sharp.'

[01:53] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Like you can crop in a lot in Lightroom, and &gt;&gt; [music] &gt;&gt; you\'re not losing any detail. Filming wide-angle video looks awesome. One of the biggest gripes that I\'ve [music] always had with the Ace Pro 2,'

[02:06] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'and just like action cameras in general, there\'s no autofocus, and they are all focused on infinity. That\'s just what an action camera does. What do you do about that? Because sometimes you want to get a close-up shot of something, and that\'s'

[02:19] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'where the close-up lens comes in handy. You actually get a proper lens cap that you can put on. It\'s just like a silicone [music] lens cap. It doesn\'t snap on, but, you know, it sits on there nice and snug, so it\'s not going to like fall off. And'

[02:31] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'that is like a big piece of glass on the front there. You want [music] to protect that, for sure. I couldn\'t find the actual field of view of this lens, um but it is very wide. So, the reason why I love this lens is for this one reason.'

[02:43] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'You can focus. When I first saw this thing, I thought it was just like, you know, you put it on, and then you get some macro shots, and then you take it off, and you put on the regular lens. This thing can actually do macro shots,'

[02:56] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'like focus really close up, or you can pull it all the way to the left, and now you\'re back to infinity. At that point, I\'m like, why would I even have the stock lens on? It gives you a shot you couldn\'t get before. That was the one'

[03:08] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'biggest thing is that when I was using this camera, I\'d always find that whenever I want to like go into details of things, you\'d lose focus super quick. Being able to actually like pull focus, and then get the exact focus that I want'

[03:20] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'to get with this thing is it\'s crazy. I love having the agency to be able to focus, because that\'s something as a photographer that I want from my camera. Switching lenses on this thing is not very fun. It\'s really stiff, and it it'

[03:33] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'low-key kind of feels like you\'re going to break it every time. Like, it\'s just really stiff. There isn\'t like a little pouch for the original lens guard. I just kind of have it in a little plastic bag in my a box. So, I\'ve actually just'

[03:45] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'kept this thing on, and it\'s been great. Like, I haven\'t really had any use case for [music] the original lens. There are a couple compromises that you\'re making with this lens, [music] using ND filters. So, I got this Freewell filter'

[03:57] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'set. So, it has a CPL filter and three different ND filters. However, they only fit on the square lens, a lens that you have to order separately with the Ace Pro 2. Usually, when you buy the Ace Pro'

